            <ArticleTitle>Promontory stimulation following labyrinthectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>729-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Promontory stimulation testing was carried out on a series of ten patients who had undergone osseous labyrinthectomy. The thresholds, discomfort levels and dynamic ranges were found to be comparable with a series of ten patients who have subsequently been successfully implanted with the Nucleus 22 channel cochlear implant. These findings suggest that cochlear implantation might be possible in a labyrinthectomized ear.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
